-- title:
--   Absolute-cursor probes define relative stopped draws
-- statement:
--   Let $b_0,t,T\in\mathbb N$, where $b_0$ is a base cursor, $t$ a suffix length, and $T$ a trial cap. Let $P$ map finite bit lists to optional pairs $(c,v)\in\mathbb N^2$. Write $w(v)=\log_2(v-1)+1$, using truncated natural subtraction and the natural logarithm convention $\log_2 0=0$. This is the trial-width bound for denominator $v$. Assume that whenever $|x|=t$ and $P(x)=(c,v)$, $$v>0,\qquad b_0\le c,\qquad c+Tw(v)\le b_0+t,$$ and every length-$t$ list $y$ extending $\operatorname{take}_{c-b_0}(x)$ has $P(y)=(c,v)$. A stopped draw on length-$t$ bit lists with trial cap $T$ is a partial map $D(v)=(h,b)$ whose returned $h$ is a prefix of $v$, whose denominator $b$ is positive, and whose value is unchanged on every other length-$t$ extension of $h$. It also satisfies $T w(b)\le t-|h|$. There exists such a stopped draw $D$ satisfying, for every bit list $x$, $$D(x)=\begin{cases}(\operatorname{take}_{c-b_0}(x),v),&P(x)=(c,v),\\\mathrm{none},&P(x)=\mathrm{none}.\end{cases}$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartAttemptDrawSites.lean#L27-L68

